# ============================================================================
#  The Microphone -- what never goes in git
# ============================================================================

# YOUR CONVERSATIONS. Every line's turns, its sandbox, its archives. This is the
# single most important line in this file: threads/ is the whole content of every
# conversation you have ever had with a line, and it is created at runtime, not
# shipped. The server recreates it on first boot.
threads/

# YOUR CONFIG. It names paths on your machine and, if you enabled the Foreman,
# which credential files it reads. Commit mic.config.example.json instead.
mic.config.json

# Your own elevated helpers. The pattern lives in examples/; what you actually
# wire up points at your accounts and is yours, not the package's.
helpers/

# Runtime state and logs -- churn, no evidence value.
day-state.json
foreman-notes.json
*.log

# The armed-turn audit trail. Append-only and worth keeping locally; not public.
FOREMAN-LEDGER.md

node_modules/
.DS_Store
